  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 106 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures around the area are in the low 60s with \nwinds out of the southeast around 10 mph. There is once again a \nchance of showers across south central SD today. The chance of \naccumulations higher than 0.10\" is around 45 to 75% along and south \nof I-90. There could be a weak thunderstorms or two mixed in but \nsevere storms are not expected. HRRR Smoke is still showing a \nmoderate concentration of smoke over our area today and Friday. This \nis mainly aloft but there could be some at the surface and \ncould cause some slight decreases to visibility. The majority of\nmodels are showing a layer of incredibly low stratus across \nmost of the forecast area later this evening through Friday \nmorning. Some short term models are also showing much higher \nceilings, including some that have switched camps from run to \nrun, so, confidence is low on how low clouds will get. \n\nSPC has highlighted northern SD in a Marginal Risk (level 1 out of \n5) for severe storms Friday afternoon across northern SD. \nConfidence is low that these storms will actually form. There \nare some CAMs that show storms over north central SD and some \nthat show storms over northeast SD. Either way, current \nprecipitation chances are 30% or less. Heat returns Friday over \ncentral SD and then Saturday and Sunday for the entire forecast \narea. Highs may be a little high over northeastern SD where \nhumidity is higher but should be fairly ok over central SD. \nCurrent forecast over central SD is in the mid 100s. This may \nnecessitate a heat advisory. Keep an eye on the forecast for any\nupdates concerning this. Highs over northeast SD and west \ncentral MN might be closer to the low 90s than the currently \nforecast mid 90s. Temperatures moderate a bit for next work \nweek. During this heat wave, precipitation chances are very \nlimited. We are, however, seeing a signal for some possible \nprecip mid next week.",
